# Never bake these into the image, and never send them to the build
# context at all. A26: this file didn't exist before, and its absence was
# a real (if narrow) build-reliability bug — with no .dockerignore, `COPY
# . .` sends whatever is on disk in `frontend/` into the build context,
# including node_modules. In a worktree checkout, `node_modules` is a
# symlink to the shared tree's real directory (see scripts/session.sh /
# CLAUDE.md's worktree convention), so the build context's `node_modules`
# is a *file* (a symlink) colliding with the real directory `npm ci`
# already populated in the `deps` stage, and `COPY . .` fails outright:
# "cannot replace to directory .../node_modules with file". A clean CI
# checkout has no node_modules at all so this never showed up there, only
# when building from a local/worktree tree that already has one installed.

# --- Secrets (supplied as Vercel/Railway env vars, must NOT ship in the image) ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Local runtime / caches (ephemeral, regenerated) ---
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.screens/
public/*.apk

# --- Dev / VCS / tooling ---
.git/
.gitignore
# Anchored to the root only — content/*.md (terms.md, privacy.md) is real
# build content the app reads at runtime (app/terms/page.tsx,
# app/privacy/page.tsx), not dev docs, and must NOT be excluded here.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/README.md
scripts/*.test.sh
scripts/*.test.mjs
